    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Supreme Council declared independence on 9 April 1991 after a referendum on 31 March, making Georgia the first non-Baltic Soviet republic to do so; its first president, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zviad-gamsakhurdia">Zviad Gamsakhurdia</a>, was deposed in a coup within the year and civil war lasted until December 1993.</li><li>Abkhazia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-ossetia">South Ossetia</a> won de facto independence with Russian support in the wars of the early 1990s, when 230,000 to 250,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a> were expelled from Abkhazia; after the war of August 2008 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> recognised both, and Georgia regards them as occupied territory.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rose-revolution">Rose Revolution</a> of 2003 turned a near-failed state into a market economy that the World Bank called the world's number one reformer, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> made Georgia a candidate in December 2023, before the ruling Georgian Dream party paused accession in 2024.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Georgia hosts the world's earliest known sites of winemaking, dating to about 6000 BCE, and the Georgian folk song '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakrulo">Chakrulo</a>' was one of 27 pieces of music carried into space on the Voyager Golden Records launched on 20 August 1977.</p></aside>
    </section>

